      <para>For questions 6 – 11, enter the coordinates of the vertex of the graph that represents the equation.</para>
      <para>Find the coordinates of the vertex for the equation \(y=(x-3)^2 + 5\).</para>
      <para> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
